outcome:
packages/core/src/pricing exposes a function to fetch a historical USD price series for a coin over a given range (24H/7D/1M/1Y/ALL), sourced the same way spot price already is (CoinGecko direct, CoinPaprika direct as fallback -- CoinGecko's market_chart-shaped endpoint and CoinPaprika's historical-ticker-shaped endpoint are the intended direct sources, but the exact request shape/pagination is this layer's own build-time detail, not fixed here), plus an estimateHistoricalPortfolioValue function matching this exact shape confirmed with the user:

function estimateHistoricalPortfolioValue(
  tokens: { balance: number; priceAt: (timestamp: number) => number }[],
  timestamp: number
): number {
  return tokens.reduce(
    (total, token) => total + token.balance * token.priceAt(timestamp),
    0
  )
}

Nothing in this layer wires the result into any UI -- that is main-screen-chart's job, depending on this layer.
